  "userStories": [
    {
      "id": "BE-0001",
      "title": "Create backend Go module layout",
      "description": "Create the backend service structure under the existing Go module without disrupting the current CLI packages.",
      "acceptanceCriteria": [
        "Create cmd/yalla-api/main.go as the HTTP API binary entrypoint.",
        "Create cmd/yalla-worker/main.go as the provisioning worker entrypoint.",
        "Create internal/controlplane packages for HTTP, config, persistence, auth, policy, quota, jobs, dokploy, audit, telemetry, and testutil.",
        "Keep existing CLI packages buildable while adding backend packages.",
        "All public responses use stable JSON envelopes with schema_version yalla.output.v1 or yalla.error.v1.",
        "Unit tests cover success, validation failure, authorization failure, and not-found behavior.",
        "Integration tests run against isolated Postgres migrations and never require a live Dokploy server unless explicitly marked external.",
        "Secrets, tokens, API keys, cookies, and rendered environment variable values are redacted in logs, errors, audit metadata, and test output."
      ],
      "type": "foundation",
      "priority": 1,
      "passes": true,
      "notes": "Completed initial same-repo backend skeleton with cmd/yalla-api, cmd/yalla-worker, internal/controlplane package layout, stable bootstrap envelopes, and focused HTTP tests. Full go test, race, and vet checks passed."
    },
    {
      "id": "BE-0002",
      "title": "Define backend configuration contract",
      "description": "Implement typed configuration for the control-plane API and worker.",
      "acceptanceCriteria": [
        "Support environment variables for API address, public URL, Postgres DSN, signing keys, Dokploy base URL, Dokploy service token, log level, and feature flags.",
        "Validate required configuration at startup and fail fast with stable error codes.",
        "Support separate profiles for local, test, staging, and production.",
        "Never log raw DSNs or tokens.",
        "All public responses use stable JSON envelopes with schema_version yalla.output.v1 or yalla.error.v1.",
        "Unit tests cover success, validation failure, authorization failure, and not-found behavior.",
        "Integration tests run against isolated Postgres migrations and never require a live Dokploy server unless explicitly marked external.",
        "Secrets, tokens, API keys, cookies, and rendered environment variable values are redacted in logs, errors, audit metadata, and test output."
      ],
      "type": "foundation",
      "priority": 1,
      "passes": true,
      "notes": "Implemented internal/controlplane/config: stable Env* var contract (YALLA_PROFILE/API_ADDR/PUBLIC_URL/DATABASE_URL/SIGNING_KEYS/DOKPLOY_BASE_URL/DOKPLOY_TOKEN/LOG_LEVEL/FEATURE_FLAGS), four profiles (local/test/staging/production) with per-profile defaults and strict-profile required-field enforcement, fail-fast typed CodeConfig validation that never echoes secrets, and Redacted()/LogValue()/String() credential-free views. Wired LoadFromEnv into cmd/yalla-api and cmd/yalla-worker startup. Unit tests cover success per profile, every validation failure path, and redaction guarantees. gofmt, go build, go vet, go test ./..., and go test -race ./... pass. goimports/golangci-lint/staticcheck not installed locally. Auth-failure/not-found criteria are N/A for a pure config contract; integration-test criterion deferred to persistence stories."
    },
    {
      "id": "BE-0003",
      "title": "Implement service lifecycle and graceful shutdown",
      "description": "Make the API and worker start, report readiness, handle signals, drain requests, and exit predictably.",
      "acceptanceCriteria": [
        "HTTP server uses context cancellation and bounded shutdown timeout.",
        "Worker stops claiming new jobs before shutdown and safely releases in-flight leases.",
        "Readiness reports unhealthy until DB migrations and dependency checks pass.",
        "Tests cover cancellation, shutdown timeout, and readiness transitions.",
        "All public responses use stable JSON envelopes with schema_version yalla.output.v1 or yalla.error.v1.",
        "Unit tests cover success, validation failure, authorization failure, and not-found behavior.",
        "Integration tests run against isolated Postgres migrations and never require a live Dokploy server unless explicitly marked external.",
        "Secrets, tokens, API keys, cookies, and rendered environment variable values are redacted in logs, errors, audit metadata, and test output."
      ],
      "type": "foundation",
      "priority": 1,
      "passes": true,
      "notes": "Added runtime.RunHTTPServer (context-cancellation driven graceful shutdown bounded by a fresh timeout context) and runtime.Readiness (concurrency-safe named startup gates). httpapi.NewHandler now takes a ReadinessReporter; /readyz returns 503 + yalla.error.v1 E_SERVER until gates pass, 200 + yalla.output.v1 once ready. New worker.Loop stops claiming jobs as soon as its context is cancelled and releases interrupted in-flight leases on a shutdown-independent context; worker.NoopClaimer is the placeholder until the durable job store lands. Config gained YALLA_SHUTDOWN_TIMEOUT (per-profile defaults, 1s-5m range validation). cmd/yalla-api and cmd/yalla-worker wired to the new lifecycle helpers. Tests cover readiness transitions, cancellation, shutdown-timeout bounding, serve errors, in-flight lease release, and completed-job non-release. gofmt, go build, go vet, go test ./..., and go test -race ./... pass. goimports/golangci-lint/staticcheck/govulncheck not installed locally. Postgres integration-test criterion is N/A for this story (no persistence yet); auth/not-found criteria are covered by the existing /readyz and route-not-found envelope tests."
    },
